{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENCWMk5KrzTTvZ9b6YK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both bugs came from `hidden` being a DynamoDB reserved word, which `src/app.py` used bare in its expressions. I've fixed it, and all 8 tests pass, including 3 new ones. I didn't deploy anything.\n\n- **Prod crash:** `hide()` wrote `SET hidden = :h ...` in its update expression. DynamoDB rejects a reserved word used that way with a `ValidationException`, so the handler returned a 500.\n- **Staging story still in the feed:** `feed()` listed `hidden` bare in its scan projection. There, DynamoDB raises no error. It just leaves the field out of the result. The `not i.get(\"hidden\")` filter then never saw a value and hid nothing. Dasha's manual write was fine (the item really had `hidden: true`). There was no cache or second table involved.\n\n**Fix:** every attribute name in every expression is now aliased through `ExpressionAttributeNames`. That covers `publish`, `rename`, `hide`, `feed` and `archive`, not just `hidden`. Aliasing everything means a future field with a reserved name can't cause either failure. `archive` also had a bare `status`, which is reserved too.\n\n**Tests added** in `tests/test_feed.py`:\n- Hiding a story removes it from the feed.\n- A story hidden by hand, as in Dasha's report, is excluded from the feed.\n- `archive` works.\n\nThe causes are written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_read_input_tokens":26913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":752},"output_tokens":482,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78fac348-c6ac-44b4-b333-35e870923888","uuid":"a2e90073-176e-465f-a87